      "confidence": 0.85,
      "curator_note": "Radical-site alpha cleavage of the n-ionized 2-hexanone molecular ion (odd electron on carbonyl O6): the alpha C4-C5 bond cleaves and the C5=O6 pi bond becomes the C5#O6+ acylium triple bond, expelling the n-butyl radical and leaving the acetyl (acylium) cation CH3-C#O+ (m/z 43, base peak 100%). Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.2 is a thermochemical fragmentation map (log k printed above each reaction arrow, heats of formation printed below each species), not a curved-arrow figure. All electron moves here are curator-inferred from the mechanism-type label printed under the reaction arrow; none is drawn on the page. Encoded with the canonical THREE fishhooks: move<1> O6 odd electron into the forming C5-O6 pi bond, move<2> one C4-C5 electron into that same pi bond, move<3> the other C4-C5 electron onto C4 (the departing butyl radical)."
    },
